# dadan-dijital Project Conventions

Always follow these conventions when working in this monorepo.

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| API | NestJS 11 · Bun runtime · Express adapter |
| Database | PostgreSQL · Prisma v7 · PrismaPg driver adapter |
| Auth | @nestjs/jwt + Guards |
| Validation | class-validator + class-transformer |
| Caching | Redis · BullMQ |
| Frontend | Next.js App Router · TanStack Query v5 |
| Monorepo | pnpm@9.15.4 · Turborepo |

## Monorepo Layout

```
apps/api/    → @dadan/api   (NestJS backend)
apps/web/    → @dadan/web   (Next.js frontend)
packages/db/ → @dadan/db    (Prisma schema + DbContext)
```

## API Conventions (`apps/api/src/`)

- **Feature modules**: each domain is a NestJS module at `src/<feature>/<feature>.module.ts`
- **Thin controllers**: controllers only parse input and call one service — no business logic
- **Services own business logic**: orchestrate repositories, own transactions
- **Repository pattern**: all DB access through repository classes that inject `DbContext`
- **Never** `new PrismaClient()` in a service — always inject `DbContext` from `@dadan/db`
- **Guards** for auth (`@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)`) — not middleware
- **DTOs** on every incoming request — `class-validator` + `ValidationPipe`
- **Naming**: `<feature>.controller.ts`, `<feature>.service.ts`, `<feature>.repository.ts`, `<feature>.dto.ts`

## Web Conventions (`apps/web/`)

- **Feature structure**: `features/{domain}/api/ + hooks/ + types/ + index.ts`
- Server components → `fetch*` functions for reads
- Client components → `useMutation` for writes; invalidate queries (not `router.refresh`)
- Shared code → `shared/lib/`, `shared/components/`, `shared/providers/`

## Database Rules

- Single `DbContext` instance — `@Global()` module in `packages/db`
- Always `select` only needed fields in `findMany()` — never select `*`
- Use keyset pagination (explicit `where` bounds) for large tables — not `cursor`+`skip`
- Define `@@index` in Prisma schema for every `where`/`orderBy`/FK field
- Aggregate with `.count()`, `.aggregate()`, `.groupBy()` — never fetch-all-then-count

## Secrets & Environment

- **Never hardcode** secrets, URLs, or credentials — use `@nestjs/config` + env vars
- `DATABASE_URL` → PgBouncer (pooled connection)
- `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` → PostgreSQL direct (migrations only)
- All secrets in `.env` (gitignored)

## Forbidden Patterns

- `new PrismaClient()` anywhere except `DbContext`
- Editing `packages/db/src/generated/` (auto-generated)
- `router.refresh()` after mutations in Next.js — use `invalidateQueries` instead
- Business logic in NestJS controllers
- Offset pagination (`skip`/`take`) on tables with >10k rows
- Committing `.env` files

## Build & Quality Gates

```bash
pnpm typecheck   # zero errors required
pnpm lint        # zero errors required
pnpm test        # all tests must pass
```

## Package Manager

Use `pnpm` (not npm or yarn). Install in a specific workspace with:
```bash
pnpm --filter @dadan/api add <package>
pnpm --filter @dadan/web add <package>
```
